{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1514588-apocalipse-wod","id":1514588,"title":"Apocalipse WoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-11T11:31:18-07:00","id":1514588,"title":"Apocalipse WoD","content":"I know that in VtM there is the night of Gehenna, in DtF them the return of the morning star that will start a fight between the fallen, WtA is literally to avoid this. But what about the other games, the mummies, the changelings, the mages, did they have any closure with an end of the world or final battle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T11:43:02-07:00","id":1514590,"title":"","content":"Werewolf wasn't about averting it. It was about fighting a last horrible battle that would most likely destroy everything. And how many different shapes would that battle take and how different the world might be even if you managed to stop some of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T11:46:20-07:00","id":1514591,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Time of Judgment&quot; event in 2003-2004 included wrap-up books for many of the supernaturals.<ul><li>January 14, 2004: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/700/Gehenna\" target=\"_blank\">Gehenna</a></b> and the associated fiction, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/3720/Gehenna--The-Final-Night-Time-of-Judgment-Act-1-of-3\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Gehenna: The Final Night</b></a> (Vampire: The Masquerade)</li> <li>February 2: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1619/Apocalypse\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Apocalypse</b></a> and the associated fiction, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/3652/The-Last-Battle-Time-of-Judgment-Act-2-of-3\" target=\"_blank\"><b>The Last Battle</b></a> (Werewolf: The Apocalypse)</li> <li>March 1: <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1718\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Ascension</b></a> and the associated fiction, <b><a href=\"http://www.drivethrufiction.com/product/3050\" target=\"_blank\">Judgment Day</a></b> (Mage: The Ascension)</li> <li>March 15: <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/699\" target=\"_blank\"><b>World of Darkness: Time of Judgment</b></a> was a big all-in-one sourcebook including end-of-the-world material for Changeling: The Dreaming, Kindred of the East, Hunter: The Reckoning, Mummy: The Resurrection, and Demon: The Fallen.</li> <li>March 15: <b>Mind's Eye Theatre: </b><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1621\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Laws of Judgment</b></a> did a similar thing from the LARP side, providing material for Laws of the Night (VTM), Laws of the Wild (WTA), Laws of Ascension (MTAs), The Shining Host (CTD), Laws of the Reckoning (HTR), Laws of the East (KotE), Laws of the Resurrection (MTR), and an Oblivion (WTO) adaption of Wraith's final book from 1999, Ends of Empire.</li> <li>March 29: <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/776?affiliate_id=13&amp;src=WWWiki\" target=\"_blank\"><b>End Game</b></a> wrapped up the Orpheus miniseries. Not technically part of the Time of Judgment, but fits thematically.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T11:48:23-07:00","id":1514592,"title":"","content":"There were four hardcover books released in 2004. <b>Gehenna</b> for Vampire, <b>Apocalypse</b> for Werewolf, <b>Ascension</b> for Mage, and <b>World of Darkness: Time of Judgement</b>, with chapters for Changeling, Hunter, Demon, Mummy, and Kindred of the East. (Wraith's ending, <i>End of Empire</i>, came out a few years before this.) You can get all of these on DriveThruRPG.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ninjad \ud83e\udd77","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T12:03:08-07:00","id":1514596,"title":"","content":"In any of these scenarios, if you can call it that, some supernatural remains, because I only know Gehenna really well and what I can say is that the most likely thing is that kindred ceased to exist as a species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T09:11:48-07:00","id":1514849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1514588-apocalipse-wod?p=1514596#post1514596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any of these scenarios, if you can call it that, some supernatural remains, because I only know Gehenna really well and what I can say is that the most likely thing is that kindred ceased to exist as a species.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gehenna definitely tends to lean that way, in the sourcebook, but really &quot;the most likely scenario&quot; is completely dependent upon the background decisions that the Storyteller makes about the cosmology and mythology of &quot;their&quot; World of Darkness. The penchant for the Cainite condition to disappear in <u>Gehenna</u> tends to be predicated upon the will of the Abrahamic God, who tends to be portrayed at least fairly analogous to the Bible version. But if your World of Darkness metaphysics include a God who is non-existent or radically different from the Biblical interpretation, then your outcome is going to change massively.<br /> <br /> I do think that &quot;supernatural creatures disappear&quot; is something that comes up in some of the printed End Times scenarios, but it's a less common feature than in the Gehenna storylines. Admittedly, plenty of them also include a world utterly ruined, nothing but a war-torn hellscape fought over by the worst monsters that have managed to survive the End of the World. I can't recall them all off the top of my head to provide more details; Werewolf and Mage got three or four each as well, and then there were close to another half-dozen scenarios in <u>Time of Judgment</u>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T10:41:18-07:00","id":1514859,"title":"","content":"I think that the most optimistic and at the same time worthy of the apocalypse scenario happens as follows:<br /> <br /> - Kindred no longer exist, after Cain finally has his second death, the curse ends and Kindred are freed from their condition, they return to being human and finally looking at the sun again while gradually aging to their true age, the who are still alive have a lifetime ahead of them waiting for them. The antediluvians go back to sleep and this time forever.<br /> <br /> - The battle against the Wyrm is won and after years the balance of the triad is restored, as their services are no longer needed, the Garou and other shapeshifters are released from their duties and now live free from rage and with the knowledge that there will be no more of them, they will be the last of their kind, even if two Garou mate they do not give birth to a Metis, but to a human or wolf, it depends on the parents, and so it will continue until one day they are needed again.<br /> <br /> - After discovering the truth about the ascension, the remaining mages have to figure out what to do with what's left of their legacies, the theocracy is in shambles and with the disappearance of the entity, there will be no more avatars, even the remaining mages, with the time, lost their avatars, it remains for them to figure out what to do with what they have left.<br /> <br /> - The changelings finally found their way back home, this makes their human and fae part separate, but not as if this were a bad thing, because as long as the glamor exists there will always be a chance for the fae to return.<br /> <br /> - The kuejin finally had their day of accountability, they now returned to the world of the dead where they should not have left and where they finally found out if they were worthy of redemption.<br /> <br /> - The remaining fallen finally got their redemption and can return to Eden, except for those who chose to remain among humans, lived the years they had left with the life they built and when the day comes they will have to give accounts as all humans do.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T06:44:26-07:00","id":1515533,"title":"","content":"I have an ongoing setting and series of articles over at <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/Aaronsmonsters\" target=\"_blank\">my patreon</a> that entertains a world after the assorted apocalypse scenarios. One is an Earth that is crawling back after the various end times forces rose. I called it The Fortean Wasteland. Below is the introduction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>SETTING INTRODUCTION</b><br /> <i>\u201cSo, then, in general metaphysical terms, our expression is that, like a purgatory, all that is commonly called &quot;existence,&quot; which we call Intermediateness, is quasi-existence, neither real nor unreal, but expression of attempt to become real, or to generate for or recruit a real existence.\u201d \u2015Charles Fort, The Book of the Damned</i><br /> It\u2019s been at least four generations since the End of the World. No one knows the exact number of years since the old world was destroyed by the \u201cOccult Apocalypse\u201d that wiped out Western Civilization. China, India, etc \u2013 all gone. Most of planet Earth is empty of (living) human habitation, the exception being the country formerly known as the United States of America.\u2019<br /> The major cities of the world have been all but destroyed, with even those cities remaining much reduced in population and infrastructure. Now all communities having fortifications, alert guards and curfews. Most people are at a Wild West level of technology (1860\u2019s). Higher technology such as radio, airships and steam cars are the product of inventors and owned by the wealthy. Transit has been reduced to animals, wagons, and the occasional iron horse. Airships are increasingly popular, as they are a safer way to cross the wastes.<br /> <br /> <b>GAME NOTES:</b> The different supernatural conspiracies of the (old) World of Darkness are mostly wiped out, having waged war on each other and tore the world apart. Now, the worlds spiritual background is in tatters, and old, primal elements are healing in their way. The many weird and dangerous creatures formerly held in check by Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, Changelings, Wraiths and such are now loose in the world, haunting mankind like they did in ancient times.<br /> Mortals do not know all of the details! Rather, everything is filtered through a hodgepodge of data and misinformation. As a general rule, I will be using lore found in Fortean accounts of the world such as Alien Abduction, Cryptids, Conspiracy Theories and similar material to flesh out the world.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>HISTORIC EVENTS (Classic World of Darkness)</b><br /> This is how the WOD settings contributed to the setting background.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire the Masquerade (Gehenna): </b>The Antediluvian vampires rose and waged war on their children. All kinds of hell broke loose here, and a great many mortals died. Efforts to fight these monsters decimated cities and clashed with other supernatural entities (see below), laying waste to large portions of the populace. Most of the Antediluvians and vampires were killed, with the notable exception of the Eldest, the amorphous progenitor of the Tzimisc clan. Now, the great clans are all gone, with only Caitiff vampires in evidence, with most living as feral predators. A few small bloodlines can be found, but these are very remote. Revenant families (ghoul families who produce their own vampire vitae) are what remains of vampire society. They view humanity as a lesser species, suitable only as pets, playthings and food. But they look human, and rule over businesses, petty kingdoms and cults.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf the Apocalypse (Apocalypse): </b>The Wyrm thrashed in its prison, eventually breaking partially free and sending armies of gross, corrupted monsters out to destroy the world. Huge monsters rose out of the Earth and seas to rampage across the countryside and through cities (often battling Antediluvians). Fomori and Black Spiral armies attacked the Garou and other shapeshifters wreaking terrible devastation. Plagues, poison and corruption soaked the land. Now the Garou tribes and the other Gaian shapeshifters are gone, with only the most feral, wild shapeshifters still lurking in the wilderness. Wyrm monsters of many types roam the wilderness, especially Thunderwyrms, Skull Pigs and assorted Banes and other monsters. The Wyld has returned in force in the form of the Fomorians (see Changeling below) and is just as dangerous. Fomori, both wild and organized are a major issue, with cannibal mutants and cunning ferectoi ruling over wild tribes.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage the Ascension (Ascension): </b>In the wake of the rising Antediluvians, the Wyrm monsters and the discovery of Nephandi corruption in the highest ranks of the Technocracy, the Union collapsed into chaos. The council of Nine fell to their own troubles, and Mages around the world (and across spacetime) fell into chaos. With the tearing of huge swaths of the Pattern Web, the high technology of the previous age is lost. Consensual reality has reverted to superstition and a magical view of the universe (with good reason). Though some true mages may exist, they are exceedingly rare and there are none of the old conventions or traditions. Hedge Magic focusing on Hermeticism, miracles, nature magic, shamanism and necromancy are the most common with Technomancers being more like natural philosophers and \u201csteampunk\u201d gadgeteers.<br /> <br /> <b>Changeling the Dreaming (The Long Winter): </b>The Fomorians, Wyld beings of the Elder Dark returned, waging war on the Tuathan Dream and the Fae. Along with all of the chaos of the Antediluvians, Wyrm monsters and mortal warmongers, the Fomorians were almost an add-on. However, these primordial monsters are the embodiment of the Wyld, the ferocious power of cataclysmic change, and were greatly needed. The fae courts and kingdoms were thrown down, and the unbridled chaos of Nightmare and explosive creativity was unleashed. Now, the Dreaming is wild and chaotic, more akin to divine madness than anything that should be in a Disney cartoon. The Elder Dark and the fae now lurk in the deep wilderness, shaping new nightmares and feeding off the terror and dreams of mortal, ghoul, fomori, beast and elements alike. Kinain (quasi-fae) are often found as mystics, magicians and go-betweens to the fae. Many fae take the form of alien like abductors, snatching humans for breeding stock and toys.<br /> <br /> <b>Wraith The Oblivion (End Game): </b>Wraith society was destroyed by the 6th Great Maelstrom and set off a series of terrible natural disasters in the Mortal World, neatly coinciding with those of the other groups. The world is plagued with zombie uprisings, flesh-eating locusts and huge numbers of wraiths, specters and all manner of undead spirits. The efforts of powerful beings such as Mummys, Vampires, Mages, mortal psychics and powerful spirit beings manage to fight off the growing threat of Grandmother at significant cost, sealing the &quot;All-Devourer&quot; away in the Maelstrom once more, though many Malfeans continue to operate in their ancient lairs. Now the Shadowlands are quiet, but the shroud between worlds is thin. Stygia is destroyed, and there is little order among wraiths, with most becoming wild specters or returning as ravening undead monsters and other creatures.<br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T14:31:03-07:00","id":1515567,"title":"","content":"I kind of liked the concept, but what's weird here is that it seems like you just had an idea of a post-apocalyptic world and tried to build it around WOD when I think it would be better solo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T15:21:21-07:00","id":1515573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1514588-apocalipse-wod?p=1515567#post1515567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of liked the concept, but what's weird here is that it seems like you just had an idea of a post-apocalyptic world and tried to build it around WOD when I think it would be better solo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just an experiment really. I used the base rules, plus psychic numina and hedge magic. The idea was to center around mortals that had to deal with the repercussions of the end of the world.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bAll of those creatures from the major splats are much scarier when you don't have major supernatural powers. <br /> <br /> I eventually used the concept to make a dark space opera using the classic WOD rules. Set after the loss of Earth, mankind is scattered, and isolated. That setting does not hearken to the WOD splats and has been quite fun.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 06-20-2023, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}